"""{{ module_title }} module (modular layout).

One package per concern, each with an ``__init__.py`` that re-exports its
public names:

    api/            the HTTP surface
    models/         SQLAlchemy entity and Pydantic wire contracts
    repositories/   data access
    services/       domain rules
    validations/    business rules a schema cannot express

Callers import from the package, never from the file inside it. That is the
whole point of the layout: splitting ``services/`` into a second file is a
local edit, not a rename that ripples through every import in the service.
"""

